a switch on a sub-64-bit integer tag (char/int8/16/32, uint8) with an UNTYPED integer-literal case emits invalid IR on the LLVM backend (the literal stays i64 while the comparison is icmp eq iN against the narrower tag, "i64 but expected i8") so clang fails; arm32 fails too. The bytecode VM, native aarch64, and int/int64 tags handle it. spec §14.10 stmt.switch.tag; claude-todo MAJOR (switch subword-tag untyped-case).
